# 0.2 (`KEYWORD-RENAME-SCOPE`): the header moves WITH the keyword. `flowline` is 0.2
# vocabulary, so a rewritten flowchart section must declare `figdown 0.2` — a
# tool that emits `figdown 0.1 flowchart` + `flowline` emits a document that
# does not parse. This input is the corpus case: a document a PREVIOUS run
# rewrote to `flowline` and left at 0.1.
figdown 0.1 flowchart
title "Already renamed, header left behind"
process a "Step"
process b "Step 2"
flowline a -> b

# A second section that is NOT a flowchart keeps its own version: the bump is
# per section and only where the vocabulary requires it.
figdown 0.1 block
node x "X"
node y "Y"
edge x -> y
